{
  "_about": [
    "The AI editor's evals: every request below runs on each of its photos in a fresh app process, and check.py scores the result.",
    "prompts: the photographer's turns, in order; a follow-up is checked against the turn before it.",
    "set: what the app must report setting, each entry one requirement and '|' between alternatives that each satisfy it.",
    "  name+ / name- : rose / fell; name>N / name<N / name=N : its new value; name[i]+ : a curve's i-th output rose; name! : changed.",
    "  A name may carry its tool, as set_tone_curve.rgb, where it would be ambiguous; * stands for any letters, as in *_saturation+ (any one of them rose).",
    "img: how the preview must change, metric followed by up, down, same or a bound such as chroma<4 (see check.py METRICS).",
    "allow: guardrails this request may break on purpose (crush, clip).",
    "dropped: why the case no longer runs; it stays listed so --quick keeps giving every later case the same photo.",
    "Prompts carry no ( ) ? % ' or quotes: adb's remote shell would read them."
  ],
  "photos": {
    "concert": {"file": "IMG20261023224017.dng", "tile": [226, 1027], "genre": "concert|stage|performance|music|guitar"},
